{"id": "EUVD-2026-93339", "enisaUuid": "89517492-2e0c-3929-9d5d-e95540f332e7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/mad: Fix receive buffer leak when PKey enforcement fails\n\nib_mad_complete_recv() initializes mad_recv_wc->rmpp_list and then runs\nib_mad_enforce_security() before linking recv_buf onto that list.  On\nfailure it calls ib_free_recv_mad(), which only walks rmpp_list and frees\nthe ib_mad_private of every buffer found there.  As the list is still\nempty at that point, nothing is freed at all.\n\nThe caller cannot clean up either: ib_mad_recv_done() sets recv to NULL\nright after ib_mad_complete_recv() returns, assuming the MAD layer took\nownership of the buffer.  Every MAD that fails the PKey check therefore\nleaks one ib_mad_private (about 300 bytes per IB port MAD, ~2K for OPA),\nand a remote node can trigger this repeatedly by sending MADs with a\nwrong PKey.\n\nLink recv_buf onto rmpp_list right after the list is initialized, so the\nerror path has something to free.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4617c9a856188674dddb0ca66979746d07688579", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e2036fb47a5b152d53eadbd35abf311bd34cc7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bad289e42f512646a988f278f536d21547df73f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/752b30e9d339008e5ce7eed412e9446078916129", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/39c4ea72a40503e102ae07e6776005f96ca078a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5091e25ec503f7fc02723ca435226467b68caac7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0d8df85db146d6275e226cb950023be69dd6c77", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3476c28c9addfa253f505e6bd87f1f5598b961d0"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98354", "GHSA-q823-95hw-ffc6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02362c64-f556-3332-a212-5518308b1b55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.13"}, {"id": "187c46bb-4c60-3574-b94a-5e12f9b9c35f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <c0d8df85db146d6275e226cb950023be69dd6c77"}, {"id": "1de26b15-e890-393c-bbd2-149cb1e95c1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "25367e5a-203c-39d1-b139-053e21a91ceb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <3476c28c9addfa253f505e6bd87f1f5598b961d0"}, {"id": "256593f4-1699-3776-ae6a-d437722a0d8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "46b788e4-e242-3b5c-b33b-9cf0b7571691", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <5091e25ec503f7fc02723ca435226467b68caac7"}, {"id": "5fcf7c3b-0a34-344b-a2be-78ce4d8d1f5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <39c4ea72a40503e102ae07e6776005f96ca078a6"}, {"id": "69995987-8688-3302-abb8-7d0c5b70dda1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <4617c9a856188674dddb0ca66979746d07688579"}, {"id": "70847a61-305c-3e76-83b2-c923696b66ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "7fc23193-49a4-3714-abc0-75c6083f0211", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <bad289e42f512646a988f278f536d21547df73f1"}, {"id": "8806538d-972a-3a95-83cf-04ed3c8fe9a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "47a2b338fe63200d716d2e24131cdb49f17c77da <8e2036fb47a5b152d53eadbd35abf311bd34cc7f"}, {"id": "942fcaea-c318-35df-a60c-14f28cc032f3", "product": {"name":